{"id": "P0", "version": 1, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "TODO: the owner states what this project is for (stub from aec init)"}
{"id": "P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Recover, connect and reconsider accumulated knowledge from conversations and documents, keeping who said what, what was decided and what was only inferred apart, with provenance", "rationale": "Provisional statement by kai#telosmith-adoption under DEC-091 (relay-kit-private ledger), from Zach's intake words; not yet in his own words for this repo. relay-kit-private kairos/intake.md (private; not checkable from here): crawl of 2026-11-03 21:10 CT, entry dated 2026-11-03, Zach: \"Chat threads as streams of information and records of decisions and information. Investigate at some point.\" (linked there to the Anamnesis experiment). Crawl of 2026-11-04 16:40 CT, entry 2026-11-04 15:22 (Knowledge Engine), coordinator's summary of Zach: investigate GitHub repos built from Telosmith and operated by agents as Knowledge Engines, where agents \"code\" new syntheses; knowledge as code, version control over knowledge. Only the double-quoted words are Zach's verbatim; the rest is the coordinator's paraphrase.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "P0@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "README.md", "locator": "L3-4", "for": "text", "sha256": "e7680cc6dcdbd9e58014631c0497ab3ff7ba3f748067a36ba1dc320c7ae83750"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Every retrieval hit resolves to a message unit and carries message_unit_id, author_role, branch_status and conversation_id; a conversation-only hit is a defect (stage-4 gap 1)", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Anchor discovery indexes every message unit including alternates, and labels alternate hits (stage-4 gap 2)", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-3", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Adjacent-turn expansion follows the anchor's own branch path and never enters a sibling branch; expansion defaults are non-zero", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Expanded ranges merge only when they overlap or touch on the same branch path, never because they share a conversation, title or project", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-5", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "No evidence quote or snippet crosses a message-unit boundary; rendered segments label each unit's speaker from source metadata (stage-4 gap 3)", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-6", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each retrieval round is a set of diagnostic objectives, each linked to a claim or gap, and every anchor records the objective that found it", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-EV-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Every evidence link carries speaker, artifact_class, local_stance, acceptance_status and canonical_eligibility", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-EV-2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Only user statements, or evidence accepted by the user with a cited acceptance unit, are eligible to ground a core claim; imported drafts, instruction text, generated summaries and unclassified pasted blocks are ineligible", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Claims are atomic and identified by immutable claim_id@revision; a revision is a new record pointing to its predecessor", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Absence from a model response never deletes a claim; unmentioned claims carry forward with a logged implicit PRESERVE", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-3", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Prior generated state may be shown to the model but is never evidence; revisions citing anything but source evidence links are rejected", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "The quote guard writes WEAKEN revisions on failed citations rather than only reporting them", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-5", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Round-0 claims pass an adjudication gate (quote guard and adversarial terminology pass) before recurrence; failing claims enter as UNRESOLVED", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-6", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Chronology claims cite unit timestamps or branch order only; evidence numbering carries no order", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-CLM-7", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "A recurrence round that retrieved new eligible evidence and produced no non-PRESERVE revision is flagged inert_recurrence for review", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-EVAL-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each pipeline layer (anchors, boundaries, adjacency, distinctness, distillation, placement, claim use, recurrence) is scored separately against synthetic gold fixtures", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Proposed in docs/design/segment-retrieval-and-claim-recurrence.md for HO-ANA-20261110-9Q72; not accepted by Zach", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-SEG-6", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each retrieval round is a set of diagnostic objectives, each linked to a claim or gap, except the round-0 seed objective, which is linked to the target phrase; every anchor records the objective that found it", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Corrects R-SEG-6@1, which excluded the seed objective described in design note \u00a73.1 (Copilot review, PR #1)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "R-SEG-6@1"}]}
{"id": "R-EV-2", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Only user statements, or evidence the user accepted with a cited acceptance unit (including accepted points of imported drafts), are eligible to ground a core claim; unaccepted imported drafts and unclassified pasted blocks are ineligible, and instruction text and generated summaries are never eligible or admissible", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261110-19", "rationale": "Corrects R-EV-2@1, which banned imported drafts unconditionally, contradicting design note \u00a74 rules 1-2 and fixture F-03 (Copilot review, PR #1)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "R-EV-2@1"}]}
